  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unseasonably mild through Friday with 2-week dry\nspell coming to an end \n\nAnomalous upper level ridging and south-southwest flow aloft\nwill maintain unseasonably warm temperatures through late week.\nMax/Min temps will be 10 to 20 degrees above the historical \naverage for the first week of November, but should fall short of\ndaily records. \n\nLeading sfc front is expected to be accompanied by a band of\nrain moving west to east Wednesday night into Thursday morning. \nA trailing shortwave trough dropping through the Great Lakes may\ninduce a wave of low pressure along the boundary as it slows \nits eastward progression toward the coast, potentially resulting\nin another slug of rain over the southeastern part of the \nforecast area Thursday night into Friday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Trending cooler this weekend with some showers \ndownwind of Lake Erie\n\nCooler cyclonic WNW flow pattern follows in the wake of the\ndeparting shortwave trough by the weekend. Latest model data\nfavors shower activity downwind of Lake Erie. NBM may not be\nbearish (cold) enough for daytime highs Sat-Sun especially over\nthe western high terrain.",
